{"id": 28, "ts": 1780441656.6862974, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019ve just heard Emily\u2019s note that Candidate\u202fD, while technically strong\u2014responding well to unexpected events, concentrating sharply, solving problems exceptionally, and taking responsibility seriously\u2014is described as moody and a \u201cloner,\u201d which raises a flag for crew\u2011cooperation. James adds that Candidate\u202fB makes nasty remarks toward colleagues, indicating a grumpy, uncooperative attitude that could also undermine the cockpit environment.\nBoth candidates therefore have legitimate concerns on the cooperation criterion. However, when we weigh those concerns against their other attributes, D\u2019s technical competence and responsibility appear markedly stronger than B\u2019s. B\u2019s strengths are his conscientiousness, stress resilience, and weather\u2011assessment skill, but his interpersonal behavior is explicitly hostile, whereas D\u2019s \u201cloner\u201d tendency is less clearly disruptive and may be mitigated with leadership coaching.\nGiven the critical need for reliable decision\u2011making and problem\u2011solving on long\u2011distance flights, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fD is the better overall fit, provided we address his interpersonal style early on."}
